of7Nl8w9lULpMq9nvO3RWAK-xpCYHhjLW28vNBE9Ga-ndT8v5ZhKzln7hnBeIhw3aijgWIJ9CcI=
iejZgihBgR5C-RILVZMH2pYjAdfienRK4ARtZ4gycaUNI-IrD4k0NVCdIwFcDT72mGOtZv7cMXX=
OMf25GXOc31Tb_QgO_8KFz0UREhDzUSjQSRRRswjq_01j0OB8iP7TSUvZPhe2ZtOvsydytfQc6E=
Q7TbTC-0t5FF0JdJxQtEjy9CoNWDx6k5THCZJkhK6RAcEwGgMbrBFKc7uJYKJ" class=3D"css=
-sdwaa1" style=3D"color:#286ed0;-webkit-text-decoration:underline;text-deco=
ration:underline">infected humans for thousands of years</a><span>, also ci=
rculating among rodents and fleas that serve as long-term reservoirs.</span=
></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 =
15px"><span>Many people associate the plague with the Black Death, a pandem=
ic that is thought to have killed at least a third of Europe=E2=80=99s popu=
lation in the 14th century. But there are still a few hundred cases recorde=
d each year, mostly in Madagascar and the Democratic Republic of Congo, but=
 also in the United States, Russia and other countries.</span></p><table bo=
rder=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"0" cellspacing=3D"0" style=3D"width:100%"><tbody>=
