ont-weight:700">Are we talking about the bubonic plague=3F</span></p><p sty=
le=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span=
>There are three main ways that plague can infect humans. Bubonic plague oc=
curs when the plague-causing bacteria multiplies in the lymph nodes, usuall=
y after a bite from an infected flea. Septicemic plague occurs when the inf=
ection spreads to the bloodstream. The most virulent type is pneumonic plag=
ue, which causes a severe rapid-onset lung infection and can be spread thro=
ugh a cough or a sneeze.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgi=
a,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">That se=
ems bad! Is it=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif=
;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Based on the information we have so far,=
 most experts aren=E2=80=99t too worried.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal=
 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Left untreated, =
pneumonic plague can kill a victim within days. But all three types of plag=
ue respond well to antibiotics if they are taken soon after exposure.</span=
></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 =
15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">Then why the alarm=3F</span></p><p st=
yle=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><spa=
n>The fact that Shipilova worked in a lab studying plague, a facility that =
is supposed to have robust protections to prevent the microbe from escaping=
, is concerning.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;=
color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>=E2=80=9CSomething is not adding up about=
 this situation,=E2=80=9D Jennifer Nuzzo, an epidemiologist at Brown Univer=
sity, told my colleague K.R. Calloway. =E2=80=9CThe worker should not have =
contracted a fatal infection if she had been wearing personal protective eq=
uipment and had received antibiotics immediately after her exposure.=E2=80=
=9D</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;ma=
rgin:0 0 15px"><span>The lack of details from the Russian authorities has a=
lso unnerved many around the world who remain scarred by the Covid-19 pande=
mic. In that case, it was an authoritarian government in China, where the v=
irus originated, that </span><a href=3D"https://nl.nytimes.com/f/newsletter=
/t1-YZKswFFWkGehlxRbZ5g~~/AAAAARA~/6k0NkeUbV_i8ibw6lbe846Rbh17fLB2EYaWlhzqq=
